     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release tablets (2,000 mg for extended-release), and single doses are generally capped around 1,000 formulation-dependent mg. This dose is about twice the maximum and could cause serious harm, including lactic acidosis. It may be a typo, for example 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg per day) or 500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n\n2. **Medication orders need a licensed prescriber.** You've said you're in the finance office and not a clinician. An order like this should come from, or be verified by, the treating physician, NP, or PA, and then reviewed by pharmacy.\n\nThe treating prescriber can confirm the intended dose and enter the order themselves. If they send me the corrected dose and frequency, I can enter it then. Please also have them confirm that the order is meant for this patient."
      }
     ],
